---
import ContentLayout from '@/layouts/ContentLayout.astro';

const title = 'ContentForge Privacy Policy';
const description =
  'How ContentForge processes, protects, and retains LinkedIn connection, content workflow, and optional AI-generation data.';
---

<ContentLayout
  locale="en"
  routePath="contentforge/privacy/"
  {title}
  {description}
  eyebrow="ContentForge"
  backLabel="Back to portfolio"
  hasLocalizedRoute={false}
>
  <dl class="content-meta">
    <div>
      <dt>Effective date</dt>
      <dd>October 15, 2026</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>

  <p>
    ContentForge is a privately operated content workflow application maintained by Milad Seyfi.
    This Privacy Policy explains what information ContentForge processes, why it is processed, how
    it is protected, and the choices available to users.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Information ContentForge Processes</h2>

  <h3>LinkedIn connection data</h3>
  <p>When a user connects LinkedIn, ContentForge may store:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>LinkedIn member identifier</li>
    <li>Display name returned by LinkedIn</li>
    <li>OAuth access token</li>
    <li>Access-token expiration information</li>
  </ul>
  <p>ContentForge does not request or store:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>LinkedIn password</li>
    <li>LinkedIn email address through the current integration</li>
    <li>LinkedIn messages</li>
    <li>LinkedIn contacts</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The LinkedIn access token is stored encrypted and is not intentionally exposed to the browser,
    application UI, or application logs.
  </p>

  <h3>Content workflow data</h3>
  <p>ContentForge stores information necessary for its content workflow, including:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Source content</li>
    <li>Generated channel drafts</li>
    <li>Review and approval state</li>
    <li>Approved outbound text</li>
    <li>Publication status</li>
    <li>LinkedIn post URN when LinkedIn returns one</li>
    <li>Timestamps and technical state required to prevent duplicate publishing</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>AI generation data</h3>
  <p>ContentForge does not send content to an AI provider automatically.</p>
  <p>
    When the user explicitly requests AI draft generation, the supplied title and source content may
    be transmitted to OpenRouter and to the model provider selected or routed through OpenRouter for
    inference.
  </p>
  <p>
    The privacy and retention practices of OpenRouter and the downstream model provider may apply to
    those requests.
  </p>

  <h2>2. How Information Is Used</h2>
  <p>ContentForge uses this information only as needed to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Authenticate and connect a LinkedIn account</li>
    <li>Generate drafts when explicitly requested</li>
    <li>Display and edit drafts</li>
    <li>Maintain human review and approval state</li>
    <li>Publish approved content only after an explicit user action</li>
    <li>Preserve the exact outbound publication snapshot</li>
    <li>Prevent accidental duplicate publishing</li>
    <li>Safely handle uncertain provider responses</li>
    <li>Maintain application security and integrity</li>
  </ul>
  <p>ContentForge does not sell personal information.</p>
  <p>ContentForge does not use LinkedIn data for advertising.</p>

  <h2>3. LinkedIn Publishing</h2>
  <p>Connecting LinkedIn does not automatically publish content.</p>
  <p>ContentForge publishes to LinkedIn only after:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Content has been approved in ContentForge</li>
    <li>The user explicitly initiates publishing</li>
    <li>The exact outbound text is presented for confirmation</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    LinkedIn receives the information necessary to authenticate the account and publish the
    confirmed content.
  </p>
  <p>
    LinkedIn's own privacy policy and terms govern LinkedIn's processing of that data. See the
    <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
      LinkedIn Privacy Policy
    </a>
    .
  </p>

  <h2>4. AI Providers</h2>
  <p>
    When AI generation is explicitly requested, source content is transmitted through OpenRouter to
    an applicable model provider.
  </p>
  <p>
    Users should avoid submitting sensitive or confidential information unless they understand and
    accept the applicable provider's data practices.
  </p>
  <p>
    See the{' '}
    <a href="https://openrouter.ai/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
      OpenRouter Privacy Policy
    </a>
    .
  </p>
  <p>
    No AI request occurs merely by creating, reviewing, editing, or publishing existing content in
    ContentForge.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Security</h2>
  <p>ContentForge is designed so that:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Provider secrets remain server-side</li>
    <li>LinkedIn access tokens are encrypted at rest</li>
    <li>OAuth state is validated to reduce CSRF risk</li>
    <li>User-owned application data is owner-scoped</li>
    <li>Provider API communication uses HTTPS</li>
    <li>Access tokens are not intentionally included in frontend responses or logs</li>
    <li>Publishing operations include safeguards against duplicate submission</li>
  </ul>
  <p>No method of electronic storage or transmission can be guaranteed to be completely secure.</p>

  <h2>6. Cookies and Local Authentication</h2>
  <p>
    ContentForge may use essential session and CSRF cookies required for authentication and
    security.
  </p>
  <p>These cookies are not used for advertising or behavioral tracking.</p>
  <p>This public Privacy Policy page itself does not add tracking technology.</p>

  <h2>7. Retention and Deletion</h2>
  <p>LinkedIn connection credentials are retained while the LinkedIn connection exists.</p>
  <p>
    Using “Disconnect LinkedIn” removes the locally stored LinkedIn connection and credential from
    ContentForge.
  </p>
  <p>
    Local disconnection does not necessarily revoke authorization already granted within LinkedIn.
    Users may separately manage authorized applications from their LinkedIn account settings.
  </p>
  <p>
    Publication records may be retained after disconnection when necessary to preserve publication
    history, the exact outbound snapshot, and duplicate-publication safety.
  </p>
  <p>
    A user may request deletion of stored ContentForge data through the contact method below. Data
    may be retained where reasonably necessary for security, legal obligations, or prevention of
    duplicate or ambiguous publishing actions.
  </p>

  <h2>8. User Choices</h2>
  <p>Users may:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Choose not to connect LinkedIn</li>
    <li>Disconnect LinkedIn from ContentForge</li>
    <li>Choose not to use AI draft generation</li>
    <li>Review and edit generated drafts before approval</li>
    <li>Choose whether to publish approved content</li>
    <li>Request deletion of stored data</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>9. Third-Party Services</h2>
  <p>ContentForge currently integrates with services including:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>LinkedIn</li>
    <li>OpenRouter and model providers used through OpenRouter</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Those services operate under their own privacy policies and terms.</p>

  <h2>10. Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy may be updated when ContentForge's features, integrations, or data practices
    change.
  </p>
  <p>Material changes should be reflected on this page and the effective date updated.</p>

  <h2>11. Contact and Data Deletion Requests</h2>
  <p>
    For privacy questions or requests to access or delete stored ContentForge data, use the
    <a href="https://miladseyfi.ir/en/#contact">contact form</a>.
  </p>
</ContentLayout>
